  "Number": 1,
  "Question": "The largest whole number such that seven times the number is less than \\(100\\) is",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(12\\)",
    "B": "\\(13\\)",
    "C": "\\(14\\)",
    "D": "\\(15\\)",
    "E": "\\(16\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "C",
  "Solution": "We need the last whole number whose multiple of 7 is below 100. Since\n\\[\n7\\cdot14=98<100,\n\\qquad 7\\cdot15=105>100,\n\\]\n14 works and 15 does not. Every larger whole number has an even larger multiple of 7. Thus the largest possible number is \\(\\boxed{14}\\), choice \\(\\boxed{\\text{C}}\\).",
